"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative introduced by Alex, with Sarah Tan as the lead. The project kick-off was scheduled for June 15th with an initial phase one budget of $500,000, though a later executive approval granted a total budget of $2 million covering all phases. The team has expanded multiple times, adding five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture in September, and later welcoming Mike Chen and Lisa Ray for machine learning and cloud computing expertise. Strategic partnerships were established with TechInnovate to aid AI research. Significant milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase, celebrated in October, and a breakthrough in predictive analytics reported in November. Additionally, the compliance plan's budget was increased to $55,000, and security protocols were updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective January next year."
